      "classification": "formalized-foundation-only",
      "scope": "Literal canonical paired input reaches an accepting representation under an exact quadratic raw-input-length polynomial. Every supplied exact n-step raw target run lifts to exactly 3 * n successful work steps. The bridge module adds symbol-preserving framer-to-simulator and verdict-indexed handoff launches; the terminal bridge appends two disjoint packer copies to one finite work table. PipelinePairedCompiler compiles that complete table to one raw machine. For every proof-bearing PolynomialTimeMachine and every canonical pair, it internally extracts an exact target prefix k <= p(m), proves target output length at most B(m) = m + p(m) + 1, and pads the complete execution to R(m) = inputFramerRawTimeBound(m) + 6 + 18*p(m) + 6 + framedOutputHandoffRawTimeBound(B(m)) + terminalBridgeRawTimeBound(B(m)). The compiled bounded verdict, no-timeout result, language acceptance, and ordinary machineOutput are exact. All 28 paired-compiler declarations, 59 terminal-bridge declarations, and 69 terminal-packer declarations have empty axiom closure.",
